{
  "_comment": "Shared golden vectors for helpers mirrored across the C++/JS boundary. The SAME file is asserted by tests/unit/test_cpp_js_parity.cpp (against the real C++ implementations) and tests/web/tests/parity.spec.js (against the real overlay JS, evaluated in the browser) \u2014 so the two sides can only pass together. If a mirrored helper's behavior changes deliberately, update BOTH implementations and these vectors. isColorDark: hex is the '#rrggbb' the overlay receives; the C++ test recomposes it into the plugin's 0xBBGGRR word. formatSecs: ms+showSign -> the exact axis label; includes the 59.96s->'1:00.0' minute-carry and the .x50 rounding boundary. cumulativeBySector/lapsAtSectorIndex/xFracForLaps: the sector-resolution chart helpers (session_charts_math.h <-> overlay-charts.js cmCumulativeBySector / cmLapsAtSectorIndex / cmXFracForLaps). The truncate-at-a-hole rule and the per-lap equivalence of the X mapping are the two places the ports could silently diverge and draw different charts from the same race. traceValueAtSector: the race-trace Y at a series index; integer arithmetic on the index (not a float lap count) so the two sides cannot truncate to different milliseconds. latestPositionExtent: the lap chart's axis-label selection; its search bound must follow the SERIES length, which is what a lap-count bound got wrong at sector resolution.",
